  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given $:$ Radius $=R$\nDistance $\\mathrm{x}=2 \\sqrt{2} \\mathrm{R}$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{B_{\\text {centre }}}{B_{\\text {axis }}} & =\\left(1+\\frac{x^2}{R^2}\\right)^{3 / 2}=\\left(1+\\frac{(2 \\sqrt{2} R)^2}{R^2}\\right)^{3 / 2} \\\\\n& =(9)^{3 / 2}=27\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
